  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, single-profile, PCA → 48.5% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality carries discriminative signal for this task. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest single-variable comparison to the existing baseline: same profile setting, a standard pretrained encoder, and no aggregation/fusion confounds. The result will (a) establish an image-only performance anchor, (b) reveal whether image features are informative at all, and (c) directly inform whether the large multimodal sub-space (configs 016–051) is worth pursuing or whether budget should be redirected to improving RNA representations. Under a tight budget, resolving this top-level modality question before committing to multimodal or encoder-specific experiments maximizes information gain per trial."
}

